<title>AUSTRALIA: SCHRODERS SELLS TOWER FOR A$150.5 MLN.</title>
<headline>SCHRODERS SELLS TOWER FOR A$150.5 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schroders Property Trust said on Tuesday it had agreed to sell the Northpoint office tower in North Sydney to Mirvac Property Trust for A$150.5 million.</p>
<p>The sale is conditional on the success of a capital raising announced by Mirvac, Schroders said.</p>
<p>Mirvac said the acquisition would be funded by a placement of 26 million units at A$1.31 each, a 1-for-6 rights issue at A$1.30 per unit and bank debt.</p>
<p>The capital raising has been underwritten by SBC Warburg Australia.  </p>
<p>Under the terms of the sale, Schroders is to provide A$2 million in income support.</p>
<p>Schroders said Northpoint was 89 percent occupied and was sold on an underlying yield before income support of about seven percent.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
